## Session 49 summary

**Major win: fixed the 90-session `cache_coherency` blocker.** Build `DBA88871` (KEEP).

**Decisive correction:** the storage backend is **LIO fileio over one coherent host page cache** (not SCST, no per-initiator cache) — so sess48's "SCST read-cache" conclusion was a dead end. The residual coherency bugs are all mxfs in-core, not storage.

**Root cause (PROVEN, raw-disk + dmesg):** the `cache_coherency` uv fail was a read-side guard misfire. The `P43-DIR-FMTREVERT-SKIP` guard (`xfs_mxfs_dlm.c` ~6837 + P43B ~7112), built for the create-only `dir_reuse` workload, **wrongly refused a peer's legitimate block→shortform dir shrink**, pinning a stale BLOCK-format inode forever (drop_caches flipped the outlier 10→0, dir size 4096→6). **Fix:** gate the guard on `dfr_dirty || (i_dlm_mode==EX)` — a PR/NL clean holder is a passive cacher that *must* adopt the durable disk; only an EX owner keeps its in-core base. v1 (`mode!=NL`) was ~15% flaky because the acquire path sets `i_dlm_mode=PR` before the reload; v2 (`==EX`) is correct (a PR reader can't hold unshared writes).

**Validated:** cache_coherency **10/10** standalone + **17/17 full `./run.sh 2 tcp` once**; dir_reuse_coherency no regression.

**Criterion NOT yet met (reliability).** 3 clean full runs gave 17/17, 16/17, 16/17. The residual blockers are `tcp_dlm_scaling` + `dlm_fairness` — **both PASS standalone, fail only in-suite (contamination)**. I traced them completely: a durable shared-dir dirent **resurrection** (the sess10/sess17 TCP double-grant / stale-cached-`i_dlm_mode==EX` concurrent-RMW root). I ruled out the read-side (`sf_disk_check`+3-way-merge already runs unconditionally) and write-side release-durability (`bast_process` flushes the shortform inode at line 4984 before unlock at 5579) — it's the deep DLM tenure-serialization problem with a non-converged GPT verdict on file.

**For the next session:** fast reliable repro `bash tests/tcp/repro_rename_drain.sh 150 8` (fails within a few iters, nlink=0 leftover both nodes). Complete diagnosis + fix direction saved in ccmemory: `sess49-ROOT-cache_coherency-uv-is-P43-fmtrevert-guard-misfire` and `sess49-residual-tcp-doublegrant-dir-resurrection-complete-diagnosis`. Cluster rebooted clean.

The criterion ("2 node dlm=tcp test 100% successful") requires the full suite **reliably** at 100%; it is not yet met, so I am not writing the marker — work continues.

